WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.125 --> 00:00:03.962
The community of first generation
and low income students at Yale is so tight knit.

00:00:04.004 --> 00:00:07.257
I have basically made all of my friends
through this community.

00:00:07.465 --> 00:00:12.012
I would say the first generation
college student community at Yale is very vibrant.

00:00:12.053 --> 00:00:15.265
I find a lot of support
with other FGLI students

00:00:15.265 --> 00:00:15.932
at Yale

00:00:15.932 --> 00:00:19.686
I would describe the first generation
community at Yale as just like

00:00:19.686 --> 00:00:22.480
people who get it.
They come from similar backgrounds.

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:23.857
They understand your struggles.

00:00:23.857 --> 00:00:24.607
Like, you don't have to

00:00:24.607 --> 00:00:28.153
explain what you're facing
because they're probably facing it, too.

00:00:28.570 --> 00:00:30.864
I was coming 2000 miles from home.

00:00:30.864 --> 00:00:34.743
I knew absolutely nobody here,
so it was nice to have some common ground.

00:00:35.076 --> 00:00:37.662
I've never felt,
you know, like I didn't belong here.

00:00:38.204 --> 00:00:42.000
Anybody who shares that identity knows
that you can go to each other

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:45.211
and feel comfortable sharing
whatever struggles you're going through,

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:46.588
and you're not going to be judged
for that.

00:00:46.588 --> 00:00:49.716
I'm still learning to this day about,
like friends I've had all four

00:00:49.716 --> 00:00:53.094
years are from a first generation
low income background.

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:55.805
It's a way for me
to sort of connect with people,

00:00:56.014 --> 00:00:58.850
and I think that's a great asset
and tool to have in my tool belt.

